    <innerclass refid="classLaboratoryAppointment" prot="public">LaboratoryAppointment</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classAppointment" kindref="compound">Appointment</ref> entity bound to the laboratories organisation and its appointment table. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This is a thin concrete specialisation of <ref refid="classAppointment" kindref="compound">Appointment</ref>. It fixes the table name (&quot;laboratories_appointments&quot;) and organisation name (&quot;laboratories&quot;), forwards a payload to the base constructor, and exposes two static permission-query helpers by calling the shared <ref refid="classAppointment" kindref="compound">Appointment</ref> implementations. It adds no state or logic of its own.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: Controllers that work with laboratory appointments construct this class so the generic <ref refid="classAppointment" kindref="compound">Appointment</ref> code is tied to the right table and organisation. <ref refid="gatekeeper_8cpp_1a2391c0b165c65deb4ad3ad19ca6dd2aa" kindref="member">PermissionManager</ref> calls its two static helpers to authorise appointment actions. Without it, the shared permission logic would have no laboratory-specific table and organisation names to work with.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>std::optional: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Static constexpr member: a compile-time constant stored on the class; it can be used without creating an object.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Inheritance: deriving from <ref refid="classAppointment" kindref="compound">Appointment</ref> means this class automatically gets its CRUD builders.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
